# ── Review captures ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `artifacts/` is the evidence trail of every director round: paired Studio
# captures and their resolution dumps. It is 241 MB of the 261 MB on disk, it
# is REGENERABLE (the capture tools and the scenario rig are both in-tree), and
# a clone of this library should not carry a quarter of a gigabyte of PNGs.
#
# The WRITING in artifacts/ is kept: the specs, the ledgers, the review packets
# and the director rulings verbatim. Those are the decisions; the screenshots
# are what the decisions were made from.
artifacts/**/*.png
artifacts/**/*.jpg
artifacts/**/*.jpeg
artifacts/**/*.mov
artifacts/**/*.mp4
artifacts/**/*.json
artifacts/**/*.log

# ONE EXCEPTION, AND THE RULE ABOVE NAMES ITS OWN REASON: "it is REGENERABLE".
# The 0.6.0 flat-render baseline is NOT. It is a frozen snapshot of a tree from
# 2026-07 and there is no tool that can produce it again — `_theme_baseline`
# renders TODAY's source. It is the only input to R9's byte-compatibility claim
# (tools/lune/check_flat_baseline compares every regenerated flat node against
# it), it is read by six gate rows, and until 2026-08-15 it existed on exactly
# one laptop: a clone could not run the check at all, and lost the claim with it.
# 409 KB, once. Its SIBLING — artifacts/rich-skinning-v2/rows/neutral-render-dump.json
# — stays ignored on purpose: that one IS regenerable, and "regenerate it" is
# precisely what the check tells you when it drifts.

# The frozen 0.6.0 flat-render baseline: immutable, byte-compared evidence that
# cannot be regenerated; the one artifacts/ file the public tree keeps.
!artifacts/theme-packages-and-skinning/final-neutral-dump.json

# build output + editor/OS noise
build/
sourcemap.json
.DS_Store

# Studio holds an open place open with a .lock beside it — never a repo artifact
*.rbxl.lock

# Python bytecode from tools/*.py — never an artifact
__pycache__/

# The sweep suite cache: one transcript per tree state, regenerated on any
# edit. Machine-local by construction (it keys on THIS checkout's content).
artifacts/suite_cache/

# The pinned SCOWL archive the example word data is generated from. 2.5 MB, and
# tools/build_word_lists.py re-downloads it on demand against a recorded SHA-256
# — the GENERATED word data is what ships, not its source.
tools/.wordlist-cache/

# The verification graph's result store: one structured producer result per
# exact input identity, regenerated by tools/verify.sh whenever an input moves.
# Machine-local by construction (it keys on THIS checkout's content and this
# machine's toolchain pins), and the whole point of it is that it can be thrown
# away without losing a claim.
artifacts/verify/

# secret-shaped files never enter the repository at all
API_KEYS.txt
*.env
.env
*.key
*.pem
id_rsa*

# run outputs regenerate under artifacts/; the tracked exceptions stay tracked
artifacts/
